            "normalizedStatus": "suspicious",
            "confidence": "high",
            "summary": "The bundle is a real local SherpaDesk backend that will create workspace-local secrets, a venv, and can install a user-level service, but the registry metadata omits those requirements and the skill claims to be instruction-only despite including many implementation files — this mismatch merits careful review before installing.",
            "dimensions": [
              {
                "detail": "Name/description match the repository contents: the code implements a local SherpaDesk ingestion/sync/analysis backend. However the registry metadata is inconsistent: it lists no required env vars/config paths and no install steps, while the SKILL.md and README explicitly require staging a SherpaDesk API key, create workspace-local state under .SherpaMind/, bootstrap a venv, and may install a user-level systemd service. The presence of many code files (client.py, db.py, ingestion, service manager, etc.) contradicts the 'instruction-only' label.",
                "label": "Purpose & Capability",
                "name": "purpose_capability",
                "rating": "concern"
              },
              {
                "detail": "SKILL.md instructs the agent/operator to create and read sensitive local files (.SherpaMind/secrets/sherpadesk_api_key.txt, config/settings.env), run bootstrap scripts that install dependencies and create a runtime venv, and optionally install/start a user-level systemd service. Those runtime actions go beyond passive query guidance and include creating secrets and persistent background processes — none of which are reflected in the declared metadata. The instructions are concrete about where secrets are stored and what commands to run, increasing the operational impact.",
                "label": "Instruction Scope",
                "name": "instruction_scope",
                "rating": "concern"
              },
              {
                "detail": "The registry declares 'no install spec', but the repository contains bootstrap.py, scripts/run.py, pyproject.toml and explicit guidance to create a venv and install Python dependencies from PyPI. Installation uses standard Python packaging (pip/venv) and PyPI dependencies (httpx, pydantic, etc.), not arbitrary download URLs. That is moderate risk (executing arbitrary Python from the bundle and installing PyPI packages), but not a high-risk remote-install pattern.",
                "label": "Install Mechanism",
                "name": "install_mechanism",
                "rating": "note"
              },
              {
                "detail": "The actual runtime requires a SherpaDesk API key and org/instance settings (staged to files under .SherpaMind/secrets and .SherpaMind/config) although the skill metadata declares no required credentials or config paths. Requesting and persisting an API key is proportionate to the stated purpose, but the metadata omission is misleading and increases the chance an operator overlooks the need to protect the key. The README/SKILL.md say attachment bodies are not auto-downloaded by default, which is appropriate.",
                "label": "Credentials",
                "name": "environment_proportionality",
                "rating": "concern"
              },
              {
                "detail": "The bundle can create persistent workspace-local state, a Python venv, and optionally install a user-level systemd service (unit name shown in docs). These are reasonable for a background sync service, but they are persistent and affect the user's environment; combined with the metadata mismatches and absent manifest of required credentials, this increases the operational blast radius if installed without review. always:false is set (good), but autonomous invocation combined with persistent service install should be considered carefully.",
                "label": "Persistence & Privilege",
                "name": "persistence_privilege",
                "rating": "concern"
              }
            ],
            "guidance": "This repository is a full local backend (not just advice) and will: create .SherpaMind/ in the workspace, store a SherpaDesk API key there, create a Python venv and install PyPI deps, and can install a user-level systemd service. The registry metadata is misleading (it says no env vars/install steps and 'instruction-only'), so before installing you should: (1) verify the skill bundle comes from a trusted source (owner and repo); (2) review scripts/bootstrap.py and scripts/run.py for any unexpected network endpoints or code paths that exfiltrate data; (3) run bootstrap and initial commands in an isolated sandbox/workspace (set SHERPAMIND_WORKSPACE_ROOT to a disposable directory) rather than your primary workspace; (4) stage the API key manually as advised and inspect .SherpaMind/secrets handling and permissions; (5) do not install the systemd service until you have reviewed the generated unit file and confirmed it only runs the venv python module and does not modify other system units; (6) search the code for outbound network calls beyond api.sherpadesk.com and GitHub issue links (httpx client usage), and confirm acceptable endpoints; and (7) if you lack comfort auditing Python code, prefer running only read-only reporting commands against a copied sample dataset or request a vetted skill bundle from a known publisher.",
